WEBVTT

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:07.000
The following program is brought to you in living color on NBC.

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:13.660
Captain's log, stardate 6010.1.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.160
While in the midst of a ship-wide systems upgrade,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:21.440
the Enterprise has been ordered to depart Starbase 37 in response to a nearby distress call.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.880
While there, I had the dubious honor of greeting the new admiral assigned to the sector.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.840
Our time together, fortunately, was brief.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:51.960
At last we are underway, though I have mixed feelings knowing we are more than halfway through

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.000
our five-year mission.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.920
With Sulu at Starfleet for command training, the promotion of Mr. Chekov to head of security,

00:00:59.260 --> 00:00:59.980
and the return of my...

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.490
former yeoman as a newly commissioned officer, it seems the more things change, the more

00:01:05.490 --> 00:01:06.230
they stay the same.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.080
Uhura, have you made any contact with the colony?

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:11.100
Negative, Captain.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.460
I'm no longer receiving the distress signal.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.870
There's an unusual amount of interference on subspace.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:18.720
Captain, you want to send one?

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.220
Mr. Spock, any readings?

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.350
Nothing yet, sir.

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:23.120
We are still too far out.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.500
Mr. DeSalle, what's our ETA?

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.540
17 minutes to orbit, sir.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:29.670
Mr. Scott.

00:01:30.190 --> 00:01:31.970
Aye, sir. I can give you more.

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.630
Increased speed to warp seven.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:34.190
Aye, sir.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.200
Captain, long-range scans available now.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:39.960
Sensors indicate massive energy discharges.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.050
Readings are off the scale.

00:01:43.390 --> 00:01:44.550
DeSalle, go to maximum warp.

00:01:44.930 --> 00:01:46.170
Lieutenant Uhura, sound red alert.

00:01:46.450 --> 00:01:48.790
Checkoff, bring phasers and photon torpedoes online.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.470
Phasers and photon torpedoes aren't ready, Captain.

00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:52.690
Anything, Spock?

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.860
I'm at a loss to explain, Captain.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:58.690
Sensors revealed two alien vessels, then they simply vanished.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:01:59.750
Two vessels?

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:01.540
Could they have been working together?

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:02.420
Oh, no.

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.760
Uhura, anything from the colony?

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.780
Subspace channels are clearing.

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:09.200
I'm receiving a transmission from the colony now.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:11.140
On screen, Lieutenant.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:12.140
Aye, sir.

00:02:13.370 --> 00:02:15.790
This is Captain James T. Kirk of the Starship Enterprise.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.500
Are you in need of assistance?

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:23.200
I'm Cal Strickland, director of this research colony here on Primus IV.

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.700
You sure took your sweet time responding to our emergency.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.520
Well, we're here now.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:29.980
What's the nature of your...

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.640
We have the situation under control now, no thanks to you.

00:02:34.150 --> 00:02:37.530
We assumed this outpost was to be under your protection.

00:02:37.790 --> 00:02:41.030
Director, it is. Now what exactly happened here?

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.240
A short time ago, a large object appears in orbit,

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.340
randomly firing at the planet.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.220
All attempts at communication unsuccessful.

00:02:50.690 --> 00:02:53.310
Director Strickland, could we please review your sensor data

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.070
as it may contain additional information?

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:58.710
I'll transmit what we have. Of course.

00:03:00.030 --> 00:03:04.510
By now, we're not too concerned about a return visit by this intruder, thanks to the Onabi.

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:05.550
The what?

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:09.720
The Onabi. At least, that's the name we were given.

00:03:10.810 --> 00:03:14.020
As soon as the Onabi appeared, this intruder fled.

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:19.080
I'll have my chief medical officer coordinate with your people and beam down anything you might need.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:23.120
In the meantime, we'll remain here on orbit in case there's any more trouble.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:29.970
Don't worry, Kirk. Fortunately, as long as we have the Onabi patrolling the sector, we feel reasonably...

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:35.500
sure that we won't be calling on you any time soon. At least not if we need anything

00:03:35.500 --> 00:03:43.410
in a hurry. Chekov, cancel the red alert. Aye, sir. Spock, analyze the sensor data. See

00:03:43.410 --> 00:03:48.160
if you can determine the intruder's course out of this system. Rand, you take care of

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:59.840
that. Yes, sir. In the meantime, I'll be in my quarters with a headache. Do we go again?

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:19.060
space the final frontier these are the new voyages of the starship enterprise

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:27.560
it's five-year mission to explore strange new worlds to seek out new life and new civilizations

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:29.980
to boldly go where

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.320
No man has gone before.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.140
Captain's log, Stardate 6011.2.

00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:41.480
We are continuing our investigation of the mysterious intruder who has been attacking ships and outposts throughout the sector.

00:05:41.990 --> 00:05:44.910
I'm frustrated by the lack of information we've gathered thus far.

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:50.660
That, and by the fact there's nothing to do but wait for the Anabi or the intruder to reappear.

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:55.600
Captain, I do not recall previously viewing this representation.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:58.270
What, Spock?

00:05:59.460 --> 00:05:59.980
The musical-

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.470
composition you have on display.

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:06.550
Oh, you mean the hymn? That belonged to my brother Sam. My mother gave it to he and

00:06:06.550 --> 00:06:11.030
Areland when they left for Deneva. What is it, Spock?

00:06:11.900 --> 00:06:17.950
I do not understand the words. Amazing grace, how sweet the sound that saved a wretch like me.

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.640
I once was lost, but now I'm found. Was blind, but now I see.

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:29.820
Spock, it's about us. It's about what we're supposedly doing.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:35.320
here, extending compassion to those in need, saving the lost, helping those

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:39.930
people who can't help themselves, and asking nothing in return. But the song

00:06:39.930 --> 00:06:43.500
would seem to indicate a deity. We're not the religious conflicts of your world,

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:47.850
what led your species to the brink of destruction. Yes, but it's the ideal that

00:06:47.850 --> 00:06:51.920
survives. Then the hymn is still relevant. I shall endeavor to study it further.

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:57.380
Your move, Captain. Come.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.540
Beware Romulans bearing gifts.

00:07:03.640 --> 00:07:04.220
My bones.

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:05.990
Romulan ale.

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:09.850
You're aware, Doctor, that Romulan ale is illegal in Federation space.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:12.030
I only use it for medicinal purposes.

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:14.010
Now this looks familiar.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:16.140
I'll have him checkmate at his next move.

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.100
Spock.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.820
You play the most irritating game of chess in the galaxy.

00:07:20.420 --> 00:07:21.260
Irritating, Doctor.

00:07:24.370 --> 00:07:24.890
Checkmate.

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:34.630
Are you sure you don't know what irritating is?

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.730
The fact that my father married a human female.

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.180
It's terrible having bad blood like that.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:42.450
He may learn to enjoy it. Someday.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:47.690
Kirk here. Go ahead, Lieutenant.

00:07:48.560 --> 00:07:51.220
Captain, receiving a message from Starbase 37.

00:07:51.620 --> 00:07:52.780
It's Admiral Leslie.

00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:56.560
Admiral Leslie? Any relation to our Mr. Leslie?

00:07:56.930 --> 00:07:57.870
It's his father.

00:07:58.160 --> 00:07:59.520
He has got to be adopted.

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:01.220
Highly unlikely, Doctor.

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:03.190
Go ahead, Lieutenant. Put him through.

00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.520
Admiral, to what do I owe this pleasure?

00:08:07.360 --> 00:08:08.320
Don't get cute, Kirk.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.570
Just what the hell is going on out there?

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:11.470
Sir?

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:14.570
I just got a transmission from Cal Strickland,

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:17.100
the director of Primus IV.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:19.570
Yes, Admiral, and about that situation,

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:22.530
Cal Strickland is one of the Federation's

00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:25.750
most brilliant research archaeologists.

00:08:27.280 --> 00:08:28.020
And he's my friend.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.440
Imagine the shock that I felt when the very star ship I sent to protect him was nowhere

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.000
in sight.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:38.030
Now you listen to me, Kirk.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.100
You find out who's responsible for this or you're going to be watching storage compartments

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:45.240
of grain for the next two years.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:48.180
Do I make myself clear, Captain?

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:50.330
As clear as can be expected.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:51.990
What was that?

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:53.760
Don't cross me, Kirk.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:59.840
If you think for one minute that you can push this at war, you've got it.

00:09:01.210 --> 00:09:05.650
Captain, I'm receiving an urgent distress signal from the transport tug, Al Rashid.

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:11.440
They're under attack near the Klaxoil Disturbance by a ship matching the description of the intruder at Primus IV.

00:09:11.680 --> 00:09:15.460
Go to Red Alert. Mr. Scott, divert all ships' power to the engines. I want warp aid.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:18.140
Lay in a direct course to the Al Rashid. I'm on my way.

00:09:18.770 --> 00:09:21.010
What about the Admiral? I'm sure he'll call back.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:26.990
Red Alert. All hands man your battle stations. This is not a drill.

00:09:30.410 --> 00:09:33.230
Red alert. All hands manned in battle stations.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:34.530
This is not a drill.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:35.290
Report.

00:09:35.670 --> 00:09:37.210
We're closing fast on the Al Rashid.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:38.670
She's reporting that she's under attack.

00:09:38.810 --> 00:09:41.410
The Al Rashid reports a second vessel moving into position.

00:09:42.070 --> 00:09:43.530
They're challenging the intruder.

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:44.970
The Onabi, I presume.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:46.780
Are we within visual range?

00:09:47.190 --> 00:09:48.290
Coming in range now, sir.

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:48.910
On screen.

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:50.490
Slow to one half impulse power.

00:09:51.010 --> 00:09:55.180
Put us between my god.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:03.000
Sir, something's jamming. A signal. Spock, any readings?

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:07.240
The intruder vessel no longer appears on sensors, and the smaller ship is moving off.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.110
Plot an intercept course. Try to hail him.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:11.980
There's no answer to our hail, sir.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:12.800
She's going into war.

00:10:13.000 --> 00:10:14.400
Lock a tractor beam on her, Scotty.

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:22.180
Aye, sir. That's got her. She's slowing.

00:10:23.190 --> 00:10:24.430
Still no answer to hail, sir.

00:10:25.120 --> 00:10:27.280
Mr. Scott, can you get a lock on anyone on board?

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.970
There's a lot of interference, sir, but I've got a lock on...

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:35.340
alert the transporter room. Mr. Chekov, have a security team standing by. Mr. Spock, you have the con.

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:57.340
Transporter room, stand by. We still have a lock. Aye, sir. Energize.

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.120
Recalibrating. Standby.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:04.210
What's the problem?

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:06.060
It's these circuits, sir.

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:08.740
We've barely tested the new transporters.

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:11.460
Readings are like nothing I've ever seen before.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:14.930
Remind me not to use that contraption ever.

00:11:27.460 --> 00:11:28.060
It's big.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:29.360
Bones.

00:11:31.470 --> 00:11:33.840
Whatever it is, it doesn't register on my tricord.

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:35.740
Please do not interrupt when I am speaking.

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:47.900
What's that?

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:51.070
As I was saying, greeting, sentient beings.

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.830
I'm Captain James T.

00:11:52.930 --> 00:11:54.880
Captain, circuits have activated themselves.

00:11:55.820 --> 00:11:57.100
Someone else is beaming aboard.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:58.850
Mr. Chekhov, secure the room.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:11:59.780
Aye, Captain.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:11.650
Was I supposed to wait till that thing was done?

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:18.710
I just have no patience.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:21.780
How was everything, dear?

00:12:22.020 --> 00:12:22.740
I am on.

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:23.740
Now, Mr. Chairman.

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:26.260
Force field's activated, sir.

00:12:27.560 --> 00:12:29.840
Aww, that is so cute.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:33.920
Look on, a force field. Shall we play?

00:12:35.440 --> 00:12:38.320
I am Onabi. You must release me.

00:12:39.300 --> 00:12:44.130
Mr. Chekov, take our guest to the brig to get a grip.

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:46.240
I'll be there later to question him.

00:12:46.960 --> 00:12:48.780
Brig? Oh, I'd love to go there.

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:50.820
Captain, this is going to be so much fun.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.680
Take me, you mad Russian.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.100
What the hell was that?

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:03.780
Chekov, get the force field on that thing.

00:13:06.400 --> 00:13:10.210
Lieutenant Uhura, I'd like you to come down to the transport room and have a look at our

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:11.270
guest on...

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:11.970
Aye, sir.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.530
Chekov, you stay here and...

00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:17.880
Aye, Captain.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:34.300
These readings are useless. We have to lower the force field.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:39.590
In a way, it's beautiful.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:40.880
Beautiful.

00:13:46.360 --> 00:13:48.240
Let's go!

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.440
Sir, be your son.

00:13:53.020 --> 00:13:54.140
Stay on the die.

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:55.060
Check off.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:59.880
See you later.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:12.240
Scott to sickbay. We have a medical emergency in the transporter room. Please respond immediately.

00:14:19.390 --> 00:14:26.480
Captain's log stardate 6012.4. The Al Rashid has received repairs and is continuing on her resupply mission.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:29.830
We've taken Anabi into custody and are holding her for questioning.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:33.280
Sir, I have Captain Jefferies online.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:34.500
On screen, Lieutenant.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.530
Captain, is everything all right over there?

00:14:38.050 --> 00:14:39.850
What the hell was that thing, Jim?

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:42.150
Came at us out of nowhere.

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:43.650
We're not certain.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:46.100
It's not the first time that we've heard about this intruder,

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:48.680
but it is the first time that we were able to see it.

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:51.650
Well, if you hadn't shown up when you did,

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:56.180
our sensors indicated the second ship for a moment.

00:14:56.600 --> 00:14:57.240
Did you read that?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:57.980
We did.

00:14:58.250 --> 00:14:59.970
We were able to bring the pilot on board.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.180
and we think the two might be connected in some way.

00:15:02.540 --> 00:15:04.440
We hope to get some answers to all of this soon.

00:15:05.130 --> 00:15:05.810
All right, then.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:08.400
Well, you take it easy out here.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.160
The ship of yours is gaining quite a reputation.

00:15:12.440 --> 00:15:13.260
So it would seem.

00:15:13.760 --> 00:15:15.880
Is there anything else that we might be able to do for you?

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:16.780
We're fine.

00:15:17.820 --> 00:15:20.820
Besides, we need to get back to Starbase 24 as it is.

00:15:21.250 --> 00:15:22.110
Safe travels, Matt.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:23.680
Same.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:43.750
or Chekhov and Uhura bums.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:45.400
Pretty shook up, Jim.

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:50.390
They described seeing visions of the ship, crew, some pretty wild stuff.

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:53.540
Whatever it was, it happened when they came in contact with Ahn.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:58.960
A device with the ability to project holograms and induce hallucinations should be considered an extreme hazard, Captain.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:05.340
Ah, hallucinations, maybe. But I've got two people in sickbay who'd swear what they saw really happened.

00:16:05.740 --> 00:16:07.560
What I want to know is who this Onabi is.

00:16:08.150 --> 00:16:10.750
Spock, have we learned anything from the sensor data?

00:16:11.160 --> 00:16:14.240
Nothing of use, Captain. The intruder ship seemed to appear out of nowhere.

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.930
Could they be using a cloaking device?

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.570
Unknown. It does appear Onabi drove the intruder ship off.

00:16:19.860 --> 00:16:23.260
If that's the case, she did indeed save the colony and the Al Rashid.

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.080
Do we have anything definitive on this intruder?

00:16:26.280 --> 00:16:29.980
If our scanners are to be believed, the size of the intruder vessel is 200 times...

00:16:30.700 --> 00:16:32.340
Two hundred times?

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:38.530
We could, quite literally, beam the Onabi's ship aboard the Enterprise, while the intruder could beam us into theirs.

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:40.680
Nothing like being in the middle of the food chain.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:46.850
Logically, there is another possibility, sir. One could assume the intruder is merely a projection created by our guests.

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:47.890
For what purpose?

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.410
Perhaps to gain whatever reward is offered.

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:55.080
Or, she could be trying to destabilize the sector and turn the neighboring planets against the Federation.

00:16:55.680 --> 00:16:59.980
Do you two just sit around all day and make this stuff up? Talk about parano-

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:02.000
the intergalactic plots...

00:17:02.000 --> 00:17:05.190
Really, Doctor? Your lack of reasoning seems more on par with...

00:17:05.190 --> 00:17:08.070
Gentlemen, gentlemen, please. We need to start working on getting some answers.

00:17:08.600 --> 00:17:11.500
Then, Captain, may I request permission to question the prisoner?

00:17:11.840 --> 00:17:14.400
Spock, that is one emotional woman down there.

00:17:15.360 --> 00:17:18.660
I'd better question her, Jim. What she needs is some good old southern charm.

00:17:19.010 --> 00:17:22.550
Doctor, your dismal record with emotional women has already been established.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.360
Why, you green-blooded, inhuman, son of a...

00:17:26.360 --> 00:17:28.560
I think perhaps both of you should question her.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:29.980
I'm sure that between the two...

00:17:30.000 --> 00:17:33.980
two of you, you'll discover who this intruder is and how will Navi manage to drive him off

00:17:33.980 --> 00:17:38.820
three times now? Well, aye sir. Yes sir.

00:18:01.400 --> 00:18:02.260
Lower the force field.

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:03.020
Aye, sir.

00:18:13.820 --> 00:18:15.800
Well, Spock, say something.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:19.610
I would say the young lady might be getting chilled by her.

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:20.280
What?

00:18:31.560 --> 00:18:33.500
Captain, our guest has managed to escape.

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:37.270
This is the captain. We have an intruder alert.

00:18:37.710 --> 00:18:39.550
I repeat, all decks, intruder alert.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.350
Mr. Rand, you have the bridge.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:42.060
Sir?

00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:44.070
You have had the proper training, haven't you?

00:18:44.130 --> 00:18:44.590
Yes, sir.

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:45.990
You are fully qualified?

00:18:46.150 --> 00:18:46.690
Yes, sir.

00:18:47.380 --> 00:18:49.640
Then I mean now you have the bridge. I'll be in security.

00:18:57.080 --> 00:18:58.260
Maintain position, Helm.

00:18:58.990 --> 00:18:59.530
Aye, captain.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:12.470
Pavel, it's good to see you on your feet again. Report.

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:15.290
Kept in. All stations reporting secure.

00:19:15.810 --> 00:19:16.910
There is no sign of an army.

00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:19.130
Mr. Spock, take charge.

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:22.230
When you find her, report to me immediately. I'll be in my office.

00:19:22.530 --> 00:19:26.630
Aye, sir. You meant check section four. The rest head aft. Check each room.

00:19:39.050 --> 00:19:39.790
What's wrong, Captain?

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:41.410
Am I not to your liking?

00:19:42.770 --> 00:19:44.270
And perhaps something more like this.

00:20:22.780 --> 00:20:23.900
from inside the captain's office.

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.820
Well, don't just stand there, Spock. Do something!

00:20:35.280 --> 00:20:35.680
Chekov?

00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.200
I'll apologize later.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:40.440
How is she, Bones?

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:42.650
She'll be out for a while.

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.280
Move her back to the brig, take maximum security precautions,

00:20:46.360 --> 00:20:48.220
and let me know when she comes around.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:48.880
Aye, sir.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:59.980
Seems a lot...

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.840
It's a little strange that a phaser set on stun was enough to disable her after all we've seen.

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:08.000
Yeah, it doesn't make any sense, Jim. But all my reading suggests that she's truly unconscious.

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:09.930
Perhaps it is another ruse.

00:21:10.560 --> 00:21:12.280
Oh, plain possum, eh, Spock?

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:14.390
Not an unreasonable conclusion, Doctor.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:20.140
Well, I'm through playing games. It's time we get to the bottom of all this before a certain admiral has our collective ass.

00:21:20.630 --> 00:21:21.010
Gentlemen?

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:28.870
Lieutenant Erichs reports to Maine Engineering. And Syntapic reports to the bridge.

00:21:31.530 --> 00:21:33.630
Scotty, if you don't sit still, I can't finish.

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:36.010
Alas, it's fine. It's just a wee bit sore.

00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:38.760
You asked for me to come down here.

00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:40.520
Now, do you want me to help or not?

00:21:40.870 --> 00:21:41.810
Aye, go ahead.

00:21:47.550 --> 00:21:48.290
There, done.

00:21:48.860 --> 00:21:51.360
Oh, Christine, that feels much better. Thanks.

00:21:51.860 --> 00:21:54.260
Now go on and make sure Uhura is resting.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:54.800
Aye.

00:22:03.890 --> 00:22:29.110
Log stardate 6013.7

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.400
there has been another incident with the device known as ON.

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:34.380
Got back from sickbay.

00:22:35.660 --> 00:22:37.060
Christine still hasn't come around.

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:39.940
She was attached to that ON thing for a long time,

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.750
but fortunately there doesn't appear to be any permanent damage.

00:22:43.430 --> 00:22:44.610
Well, how about Uhura?

00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:45.920
Back on duty.

00:22:46.500 --> 00:22:48.380
Makes you wish you had a ship's counselor on board.

00:22:49.270 --> 00:22:51.830
Captain, I'm growing rather bored in here.

00:22:51.990 --> 00:22:53.150
Can we please move on?

00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:54.780
Lower the force field.

00:22:56.270 --> 00:22:59.980
Captain Kirk, may I first apologize for my...

00:23:00.410 --> 00:23:02.040
I meant you no harm.

00:23:02.100 --> 00:23:02.860
Nor are we to you.

00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:08.320
We simply want to learn more about you and about this alien intruder that seems to be

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:09.240
menacing this sector.

00:23:10.170 --> 00:23:10.550
Yes.

00:23:11.360 --> 00:23:12.120
The Monap.

00:23:13.020 --> 00:23:13.460
The what?

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:14.980
The Monap Doctor.

00:23:16.420 --> 00:23:17.800
A most despicable menace.

00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:22.760
I have roamed the galaxy since before your sun burnt hot in space.

00:23:23.420 --> 00:23:24.400
But soon my journey ends.

00:23:24.880 --> 00:23:26.880
So you can destroy this Monap?

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:28.210
Destroy?

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:29.450
No.

00:23:30.250 --> 00:23:33.750
But contain the monap I can, and once contained, the menace shall end.

00:23:34.420 --> 00:23:36.360
I must say, this all sounds rather epic.

00:23:36.660 --> 00:23:39.580
But there's just too many aspects that don't add up.

00:23:40.160 --> 00:23:43.340
Your vessel is simply too small to drive off an intruder of this size.

00:23:43.660 --> 00:23:46.200
Do not believe what only your eyes tell you, Captain.

00:23:46.830 --> 00:23:49.370
I think you'll find not all is as it seems.

00:23:50.830 --> 00:23:52.510
Angels and ministers of grace.

00:23:53.020 --> 00:23:53.900
Let's go up to the Captain.

00:23:54.970 --> 00:23:56.030
Kirk here, go ahead, Scotty.

00:23:56.260 --> 00:23:58.040
We're discharging energy into the disturbance.

00:23:58.500 --> 00:23:59.960
There's no reason for it, but a top...

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:01.960
Where's it coming from?

00:24:02.720 --> 00:24:05.500
Instruments read that the discharge began near the warp nacelles.

00:24:06.410 --> 00:24:08.790
I'll have to take the mains offline to run a full diagnostic.

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:10.350
All right, Scotty, I'm on my way.

00:24:10.490 --> 00:24:10.810
Aye, sir.

00:24:10.970 --> 00:24:11.330
Kirk out.

00:24:12.180 --> 00:24:14.880
Onabi, I'm going to have to ask you to wait here.

00:24:16.440 --> 00:24:18.660
If you do not release me, you will be sorry.

00:24:19.490 --> 00:24:22.250
The only thing he's sorry about is pulling duty in this quadrant.

00:24:34.190 --> 00:24:35.310
Status report, Mr. Scott.

00:24:35.660 --> 00:24:37.420
Sir, we've had to take the mains offline.

00:24:37.700 --> 00:24:39.280
The ship's running on battery power only.

00:24:39.480 --> 00:24:44.220
At our present rate of power consumption, we can maintain ship status for 3.24 hours.

00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:45.740
It should not be occurring.

00:24:46.750 --> 00:24:48.870
It is my theory there is no actual power drain.

00:24:49.250 --> 00:24:50.190
Are you a daft man?

00:24:50.370 --> 00:24:51.510
The indicators show otherwise.

00:24:51.950 --> 00:24:53.510
Would you care to elaborate, Mr. Spock?

00:24:53.740 --> 00:24:58.760
Due to the nature of awe, it could be some ploy to make us believe there is a power drain when none actually exists.

00:24:59.140 --> 00:24:59.880
But for what purpose?

00:25:00.000 --> 00:25:02.720
Perhaps to give Onabi a chance to save us.

00:25:03.090 --> 00:25:06.790
Mr. Spock, you've been able to mind meld with intelligent machines before.

00:25:07.110 --> 00:25:09.150
Is there any chance you could make contact with Ahn?

00:25:09.270 --> 00:25:12.450
Captain, considering the effect that contact with Ahn has had so far,

00:25:12.550 --> 00:25:14.710
do you think it wise to deliberately touch that thing?

00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:18.440
While the risk is great, the danger Ahn could pose to the Enterprise is greater.

00:25:18.820 --> 00:25:21.760
Captain, I believe this is our best course to understand what has been happening.

00:25:22.200 --> 00:25:25.500
Mr. Scott, Spock and I are going to deal with Ahn. Rand maintain our position here.

00:25:26.070 --> 00:25:26.410
Aye, sir.

00:25:26.490 --> 00:25:26.850
Aye, sir.

00:25:28.680 --> 00:25:29.320
Scott Engineering.

00:25:30.000 --> 00:25:33.480
I need a team to assist me near the main junction circuitry at the Matar-Anti-Matter chamber.

00:25:39.460 --> 00:25:40.440
Ahn, this is Captain Kirk.

00:25:40.990 --> 00:25:41.730
Yes, Captain.

00:25:42.480 --> 00:25:44.120
Mr. Spock may touch my mind.

00:25:44.260 --> 00:25:46.800
It is impressive that you knew of our goal before we told you.

00:25:48.120 --> 00:25:49.280
How did you come by this knowledge?

00:25:49.580 --> 00:25:53.390
I guess we're just going to have to get the answers for ourselves.

00:25:53.770 --> 00:25:54.780
Be careful, Spock.

00:25:58.840 --> 00:25:59.980
Ahn, stop what you're doing!

00:26:00.350 --> 00:26:00.710
Spock!

00:26:04.040 --> 00:26:07.900
Captain, with your permission, I shall now discuss these fuel equations with the engineer.

00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:11.870
Spock, welcome aboard.

00:26:13.710 --> 00:26:22.730
Spock, long, usper.

00:26:24.890 --> 00:26:25.110
No.

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:31.020
Don't you remember?

00:26:31.400 --> 00:26:31.800
Ship.

00:26:32.300 --> 00:26:33.100
Out of danger.

00:26:34.210 --> 00:26:34.990
You saved the ship.

00:26:35.460 --> 00:26:36.220
You saved us all.

00:26:36.700 --> 00:26:37.520
Don't you remember?

00:26:39.260 --> 00:26:39.540
No.

00:26:39.780 --> 00:26:40.060
Yes.

00:26:40.260 --> 00:26:40.420
No.

00:26:40.620 --> 00:26:40.900
Yes.

00:26:41.320 --> 00:26:42.060
I love Italian.

00:26:42.660 --> 00:26:43.240
And so do you.

00:26:44.630 --> 00:26:44.910
Yes.

00:26:46.130 --> 00:26:49.140
I thought I was going to die.

00:26:49.610 --> 00:26:50.290
Not possible.

00:26:50.970 --> 00:26:51.690
You were never alone.

00:26:51.980 --> 00:26:52.560
I thought I was going to die.

00:26:53.250 --> 00:26:54.110
Don't believe them.

00:26:54.290 --> 00:26:55.170
Don't trust them.

00:26:56.130 --> 00:26:56.850
They are dying.

00:26:57.420 --> 00:26:58.120
Let them die.

00:27:01.530 --> 00:27:02.070
It was.

00:27:11.950 --> 00:27:14.180
Gentlemen, Captain Kirk is alive.

00:27:21.990 --> 00:27:22.190
Fuck.

00:27:23.060 --> 00:27:24.220
I'm undamaged, physically.

00:27:25.780 --> 00:27:26.640
How'd you get down here?

00:27:26.780 --> 00:27:29.580
Can you explain what just happened?

00:27:30.350 --> 00:27:32.610
Those images were of no memories that I ever recall.

00:27:33.250 --> 00:27:34.390
On gave you a gift, Captain.

00:27:34.590 --> 00:27:36.450
Do you not recognize your own ambition?

00:27:36.650 --> 00:27:39.210
I fail to see how answering in riddles will accomplish anything.

00:27:40.100 --> 00:27:42.440
Those images that were shown to us, were they the future?

00:27:42.660 --> 00:27:44.640
The future is not written, Mr. Spock.

00:27:45.910 --> 00:27:48.390
As to what you saw, I have no control over On.

00:27:48.570 --> 00:27:49.670
No control over On?

00:27:50.030 --> 00:27:52.170
Then that means that thing is a danger to the Enterprise.

00:27:52.800 --> 00:27:54.860
Captain, do you not see we are the same?

00:27:55.660 --> 00:27:57.200
On is younger, but we are the same.

00:27:57.550 --> 00:27:59.390
The threat is not from us, Captain Kirk.

00:27:59.490 --> 00:27:59.970
The threat is from...

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.700
without we have found no physical evidence of your intruder in addition it is highly probable

00:28:04.700 --> 00:28:09.560
that on is directly affecting ship operations that in itself is reason enough to consider both

00:28:09.560 --> 00:28:16.590
he and yourself the true threat you believe me to be a threat you have no idea what's out there

00:28:16.590 --> 00:28:26.690
the green the cardassians the hirogen the dominion try to make friends get ready captain

00:28:26.690 --> 00:28:29.920
none compared to the monat we don't respond well to threat

00:28:32.120 --> 00:28:34.490
All of your battle stations.

00:28:34.650 --> 00:28:35.790
This is the captain. Report.

00:28:36.340 --> 00:28:39.240
Captain, the Intruder has returned and is engaging.

00:28:42.720 --> 00:28:43.920
I'm on my way to the bridge.

00:28:44.080 --> 00:28:49.240
I hope he's up for the game.

00:29:05.980 --> 00:29:10.340
Sir, shields are at 50%. Another few hits like that and we'll lose them altogether.

00:29:10.880 --> 00:29:13.120
I've ordered Mr. Scott to bring the mains back online.

00:29:16.430 --> 00:29:19.320
What's she doing up here? Just keep her out of the way.

00:29:19.680 --> 00:29:23.320
Mr. DeSalle, course 213 Mark IV. Three-quarters impulse power.

00:29:23.560 --> 00:29:25.440
Aye, sir. Lieutenant Uhura. Anything?

00:29:25.850 --> 00:29:27.710
Negative, sir. Hailing on all channels.

00:29:27.990 --> 00:29:29.750
They're coming for another pass. Hang on.

00:29:32.840 --> 00:29:35.140
Take evasive action. Get us out of that thing's line of fire.

00:29:35.660 --> 00:29:35.980
Aye, sir.

00:29:43.590 --> 00:29:47.480
Captain, we will not survive another hit like that. We've got batteries only.

00:29:48.490 --> 00:29:49.850
Scotty, I need emergency power.

00:29:50.150 --> 00:29:51.530
Aye, sir. I'm working on it.

00:29:51.670 --> 00:29:56.050
Captain, I'm receiving damage reports from all over the ship. Medical teams are responding.

00:29:56.800 --> 00:29:59.980
Captain, if we maintain this course, we will enter the Klaxoil Disturbance.

00:30:00.060 --> 00:30:01.660
our shields and sensors will be useless.

00:30:01.980 --> 00:30:04.480
And so will the Monavs. Take us in, Mr. DeSalle.

00:30:04.740 --> 00:30:05.100
Aye, sir.

00:30:06.690 --> 00:30:07.630
Aren't we going to fight?

00:30:08.070 --> 00:30:10.470
This isn't a fight we can win. This is about survival.

00:30:11.070 --> 00:30:12.970
Take us as far in as we can go, Mr. DeSalle.

00:30:13.450 --> 00:30:16.210
Aye, sir. Entering the Klaxoer disturbance now.

00:30:26.340 --> 00:30:27.460
Spock, anything on the sensors?

00:30:28.770 --> 00:30:29.980
Negative. As I warn-

00:30:30.000 --> 00:30:31.300
The orange sensors are inoperative.

00:30:31.680 --> 00:30:33.220
Communications are down as well, Captain.

00:30:34.000 --> 00:30:35.060
Mr. Scott, report.

00:30:35.530 --> 00:30:36.550
The mains are back online.

00:30:36.820 --> 00:30:39.020
Seems there was nothing wrong as Mr. Spock suggested.

00:30:40.590 --> 00:30:46.100
What's that?

00:30:46.880 --> 00:30:48.980
The Monat is trying to determine your location

00:30:48.980 --> 00:30:51.600
by setting off anti-matter charges within the disturbance.

00:30:52.220 --> 00:30:53.600
That means his sensors are down too.

00:30:54.000 --> 00:30:56.500
Spock, can you track where that weapons fire is coming from?

00:30:56.940 --> 00:30:59.980
Our deflector screens are directing particles in such a way that we...

00:31:00.000 --> 00:31:06.660
be able to get a general idea of where the intruder is how general within a kilometer it would appear

00:31:06.660 --> 00:31:13.560
i owe you an apology and i'm needed captain of course what you do next will determine your fate

00:31:13.560 --> 00:31:24.410
with the word you will either do or save your shipping crew let me help rand do we have enough

00:31:24.410 --> 00:31:29.890
power to transport on and onabi back to their vessel barely sir funnel all ships power including

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:36.070
life support to the transporter room sir do it it may be our only hope mr. Spock would you please

00:31:36.070 --> 00:31:53.820
escort Onami to the transporter room aye sir anything ran too much interference sir you

00:31:54.860 --> 00:31:59.890
performed rather well while in command you kept your head in a crisis that's the first major

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:04.450
Every test every commander has to face, knowing whether or not you'll rise to the occasion or freeze.

00:32:05.070 --> 00:32:05.550
Well done.

00:32:05.810 --> 00:32:06.850
Thank you, Captain Kirk.

00:32:07.900 --> 00:32:09.340
Uhura, raise the transporter room.

00:32:09.520 --> 00:32:09.980
Aye, sir.

00:32:11.010 --> 00:32:12.010
Transporter room, report!

00:32:12.430 --> 00:32:13.110
Spock here.

00:32:13.610 --> 00:32:14.490
We're almost ready.

00:32:15.370 --> 00:32:16.970
Onabi is communicating with Ahn now.

00:32:17.430 --> 00:32:19.830
One could describe them as being happy to see each other.

00:32:20.840 --> 00:32:21.760
We're ready now, sir.

00:32:23.310 --> 00:32:25.740
Mr. Spock, peace among life.

00:32:26.460 --> 00:32:27.520
Live long and prosper.

00:32:36.590 --> 00:32:39.170
Seven years, what a waste.

00:32:40.750 --> 00:32:40.970
On?

00:32:45.660 --> 00:32:46.700
Well done, Mr. Kyle.

00:32:47.310 --> 00:32:49.260
You too, sir.

00:32:51.530 --> 00:32:52.510
Transport complete, Captain.

00:32:53.380 --> 00:32:54.180
Very good, Spock.

00:32:54.260 --> 00:32:55.640
Now get back up here on the double.

00:32:56.080 --> 00:32:56.520
Affirmative.

00:33:01.920 --> 00:33:05.620
Captain, I'm receiving a very weak signal from Monabe. It's audio only.

00:33:06.220 --> 00:33:07.060
Let's hear it, Lieutenant.

00:33:08.000 --> 00:33:14.230
Captain Kirk, if you'd be so kind as to move your ship to 127 Mark III, I think we'd get this taken care of.

00:33:14.750 --> 00:33:16.070
Mr. DeSalle, land a course.

00:33:16.720 --> 00:33:18.980
That course will take us back to the edge of the disturbance, sir.

00:33:19.180 --> 00:33:19.940
Go, DeSalle!

00:33:30.380 --> 00:33:32.420
Sir, the intruder is right on our tail.

00:33:32.620 --> 00:33:40.300
To DeSalle, bring us about.

00:33:40.590 --> 00:33:42.730
Check out fire phasers and photon torpedoes.

00:33:42.810 --> 00:33:44.450
Firing all phasers. Torpedoes away.

00:33:52.080 --> 00:33:53.180
There's no effect, sir.

00:34:03.900 --> 00:34:06.620
Uhura, jettison the log boom, signal all hands to a panther.

00:34:07.150 --> 00:34:07.950
Stand by, Uhura.

00:34:16.200 --> 00:34:17.880
Spock, are the sensors back online?

00:34:18.500 --> 00:34:19.180
Affirmative, sir.

00:34:19.780 --> 00:34:22.780
I'm reading no sign of the intruder or of Onabi.

00:34:22.980 --> 00:34:23.920
Can you track her course?

00:34:24.760 --> 00:34:26.120
Relaying coordinates to the helm now.

00:34:27.180 --> 00:34:28.700
Tassel, follow that ship.

00:34:36.840 --> 00:34:37.840
Warp drive is down, sir.

00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:39.870
Scotty, report.

00:34:40.720 --> 00:34:42.720
Aye, the mains are down, and it's time for certain.

00:34:42.920 --> 00:34:44.660
It'll take several hours to repair, sir.

00:34:46.550 --> 00:34:47.210
So that's it?

00:34:48.230 --> 00:34:48.850
It's over?

00:34:49.430 --> 00:34:51.610
It would appear so, Rand, at least for now.

00:34:52.270 --> 00:34:53.650
Mr. Spock, anything from the sensors?

00:34:54.170 --> 00:34:54.830
Negative, Captain.

00:34:55.140 --> 00:34:57.660
There's no sign of Onabi, or the intruder.

00:34:58.430 --> 00:34:59.970
Looks like Onabi had one last trick.

00:35:00.760 --> 00:35:05.550
Mr. Ran, have Scotty begin damage control. Keep on him.

00:35:05.880 --> 00:35:08.520
Don't let him fool you with those factor of four-time estimates.

00:35:08.800 --> 00:35:09.220
Aye, sir.

00:35:09.440 --> 00:35:10.120
You have the bridge.

00:35:10.670 --> 00:35:14.170
Lieutenant Uhura, code to Starfleet Command by past week's log entries.

00:35:14.640 --> 00:35:15.920
Mr. Spock, you're with me.

00:35:16.300 --> 00:35:16.720
Aye, sir.

00:35:23.300 --> 00:35:26.440
Caracaners, report to Mr. Scott in engineering immediately.

00:35:27.030 --> 00:35:29.390
All hands stand down for red alert.

00:35:37.040 --> 00:35:40.140
Captain's personal log, stardate 6014.3.

00:35:40.690 --> 00:35:42.530
We continue to clean up our battle damage,

00:35:42.760 --> 00:35:44.880
and repairs to the warp drive are nearly complete.

00:35:45.620 --> 00:35:49.780
The ship and crew have performed well during this rather unique mission.

00:35:59.020 --> 00:35:59.960
You're playing, Spock.

00:36:00.670 --> 00:36:01.490
It sounds familiar.

00:36:01.930 --> 00:36:03.630
A hymn, Doctor, from Old Earth.

00:36:04.240 --> 00:36:06.100
The captain recently introduced me to it.

00:36:06.460 --> 00:36:08.880
I find the tune most comforting.

00:36:13.260 --> 00:36:13.820
What do you remember?

00:36:14.100 --> 00:36:14.900
Anything specific?

00:36:15.320 --> 00:36:18.020
Images mostly bones, there's just nothing concrete.

00:36:18.620 --> 00:36:20.520
If it was indeed a glimpse at our future,

00:36:20.850 --> 00:36:22.810
perhaps we should re-examine some of our methods.

00:36:23.270 --> 00:36:24.710
One possible glimpse, Spock.

00:36:25.110 --> 00:36:26.770
Onabi said the future is not yet written.

00:36:27.480 --> 00:36:29.960
Maybe what we saw was just one possible outcome?

00:36:30.440 --> 00:36:34.740
Perhaps, as the hymn says, tis grace that's brought us safe thus far, Captain.

00:36:34.940 --> 00:36:36.590
That's it, Spock. You got it.

00:36:36.860 --> 00:36:38.600
Well, there's hope for him yet.

00:36:40.540 --> 00:36:43.160
Of course. On the other hand, by changing...

00:36:43.160 --> 00:36:45.650
What was it, Spock? Our methods?

00:36:46.310 --> 00:36:48.490
That could be what causes what you saw to come true.

00:36:49.310 --> 00:36:51.150
The Doctor makes an almost logical deduction.

00:36:51.880 --> 00:36:53.920
It would appear the timeline has been altered already.

00:36:54.960 --> 00:36:56.120
Was that a joke, Spock?

00:36:56.620 --> 00:36:57.880
It seemed like a joke.

00:36:59.240 --> 00:36:59.960
I'm still puzz...

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:02.980
as to the nature of the intruder, if not a holographic image,

00:37:03.160 --> 00:37:05.160
they could be a major threat to the Federation.

00:37:05.520 --> 00:37:08.300
Well, maybe what we saw was the vision of a future invader.

00:37:08.460 --> 00:37:09.340
God, I hope not.

00:37:10.000 --> 00:37:11.760
But I wouldn't mind running into Onabi again.

00:37:12.360 --> 00:37:14.140
Gentlemen, that is for the future to decide.

00:37:14.630 --> 00:37:17.050
A future, I hope, with many possibilities.

00:37:18.530 --> 00:37:21.470
Captain Kirk, Admiral Leslie is calling on subspace.

00:37:21.710 --> 00:37:23.570
He insists on speaking with you.

00:37:24.350 --> 00:37:25.110
Put him through, Lieutenant.

00:37:26.220 --> 00:37:26.560
Captain?

00:37:27.670 --> 00:37:29.510
Admiral, I was just about to send you my report.

00:37:30.120 --> 00:37:34.010
Fine, Kirk. In the meantime, let me tell you about your next assignment.

00:37:34.750 --> 00:37:36.050
We're all ears, sir.

00:37:38.820 --> 00:37:50.100
You will proceed to the following coordinates and rendezvous with two robot cargo ships carrying a shipment of grain to Sherman's planet.

00:37:51.120 --> 00:37:53.490
Admiral, may I just say on our behalf that...

00:37:53.490 --> 00:37:58.530
Oh, no, Kirk. Oh, no. Wait. There's more.

00:38:00.670 --> 00:38:00.970
Good boy.

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:30.240
Thank you.
